<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marie of Montpellier</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1182–1213</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marie of Montpellier was the heiress of the lordship of Montpellier and Queen of Aragon. In 1204 she married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-ii-of-aragon">Peter II of Aragon</a>, bringing Montpellier to the Crown of Aragon, and in 1208 she gave birth there to the future <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I of Aragon</a>. The marriage was unhappy, and she died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 1213 while defending it before the Pope.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marie-of-montpellier.jpg" alt="Marie of Montpellier" width="318" height="278" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pedro2_marie.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
